.TH SDL_GetPlatform 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetPlatform \- Get the name of the platform.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_platform.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_GetPlatform(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Here are the names returned for some (but not all) supported platforms:
.PP

\(bu \(dqWindows\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqmacOS\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqLinux\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqiOS\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqAndroid\(dq

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the name of the platform\[char46] If the correct platform name is not available, returns a string beginning with the text \(dqUnknown\(dq\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

